  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Cossinfo — Lottery Store Automation Platform",
    "description": "Product Builder | lottoautomation.cossinfo.com\nLottery retail stores in Australia run on a patchwork of manual processes — paper rosters, manual till reconciliation, disconnected syndicate tracking, and spreadsheet-based timesheets. I set out to understand this problem end-to-end and build a single platform to solve it.\nProblem discovery:\nResearched how lottery stores actually operate day-to-day — where staff lost time, where errors crept in (till discrepancies, missed syndicate commitments, inconsistent scratch ticket tracking), and where owners lacked visibility across locations.\nSolution approach:\nDesigned and built Cossinfo, an all-in-one automation platform, rather than a single-feature tool — because the real pain point was operations being scattered across too many systems. Used an AI-assisted (\"vibe coding\") development approach to move from concept to working product quickly, focusing my own effort on problem definition, workflow design, and product decisions rather than manual coding.\nKey features shipped:\nGroup Syndicate Marketplace — lets stores list, discover, and commit to lottery syndicates fast\nRostering — staff scheduling in one place\nTill Close & Coin Orders — automated daily reconciliation\nScratch Ticket Tracking — inventory visibility\nEmployee Timesheets — replacing manual/paper tracking\nOutcome:\nA live, functioning platform built and launched independently — from identifying a real operational gap in an underserved retail niche to shipping a working product store owners can actually use.",
